WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.389 --> 00:00:02.217
- I'm generally pretty hardcore.

00:00:02.217 --> 00:00:03.078
I want a hard race,

00:00:03.078 --> 00:00:04.271
I want to be destroyed afterwards.

00:00:04.271 --> 00:00:06.927
My dad would say, "My son's going to be

00:00:06.927 --> 00:00:08.075
"the first black Formula One driver".

00:00:08.075 --> 00:00:09.818
Everyone thought, "Yeah right".

00:00:09.818 --> 00:00:12.609
We harness energy without even noticing it

00:00:12.609 --> 00:00:14.142
and whether it's good or bad.

00:00:14.142 --> 00:00:17.843
My goal this weekend, is to win this race.

00:00:17.843 --> 00:00:20.406
All the other stuff is all just noise.

00:00:20.406 --> 00:00:21.747
- He's a British Formula One

00:00:21.747 --> 00:00:23.799
race car driver, currently racing with

00:00:23.799 --> 00:00:26.283
the Mercedes AMG Petronas Team.

00:00:26.283 --> 00:00:28.533
He's a 2008, 2014, and 2015

00:00:29.697 --> 00:00:31.617
Formula One World Champion.

00:00:31.617 --> 00:00:33.526
He's the only driver in
this history of the sport

00:00:33.526 --> 00:00:35.283
to have won at least one race

00:00:35.283 --> 00:00:37.337
in each of the season's he's competed in.

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:38.360
He's Lewis Hamilton

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:41.117
and here's my take on his
top 10 rules for success.

00:00:41.117 --> 00:00:42.525
Rule number one is my personal favorite

00:00:42.525 --> 00:00:44.210
and make sure to stick
around all the way to the end

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:45.971
for some special bonus clips.

00:00:45.971 --> 00:00:48.142
And as always, if Lewis says
something that really, really

00:00:48.142 --> 00:00:50.833
resonates with you, please
leave it in the comments below

00:00:50.833 --> 00:00:51.794
and put quotes around it,

00:00:51.794 --> 00:00:54.072
so other people can be inspired as well.

00:00:54.072 --> 00:00:54.905
Enjoy!

00:00:58.059 --> 00:01:00.809
(dramatic music)

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:09.977
- The first year was...

00:01:11.657 --> 00:01:13.282
the first year, I met McLaren.

00:01:13.282 --> 00:01:15.206
I've got the two time World Champion.

00:01:15.206 --> 00:01:17.659
He just won the Championship 2006, 2007,

00:01:17.659 --> 00:01:19.883
he's got number one on his
car, I'm going to be number 2,

00:01:19.883 --> 00:01:22.133
because that's how it goes.

00:01:23.077 --> 00:01:24.881
I remember sitting,

00:01:24.881 --> 00:01:26.560
testing, just studying,
studying, studying.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:29.200
I've got to make sure that

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:31.743
I somehow would have matched this guy.

00:01:31.743 --> 00:01:33.781
I believe in myself that I'm...

00:01:33.781 --> 00:01:36.357
Somewhere in me, there's
the speed to keep up

00:01:36.357 --> 00:01:37.885
and beat this guy.

00:01:37.885 --> 00:01:42.052
So, before the first race,
Ron said in his office,

00:01:43.897 --> 00:01:45.538
"You got to expect and don't be surprised

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:49.625
if you're half a second behind
Fernando at the first race."

00:01:49.625 --> 00:01:51.386
You don't know what that did to me inside.

00:01:51.386 --> 00:01:52.397
I was so...

00:01:52.397 --> 00:01:53.364
- What did it do?

00:01:53.364 --> 00:01:55.964
- It just boiled me inside

00:01:55.964 --> 00:01:58.060
because he obviously undervalued...

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:00.171
Not undervalued me, because
he obviously gave me the role,

00:02:00.171 --> 00:02:04.123
but he was not expecting me to be able

00:02:04.123 --> 00:02:06.873
to answer to his special new guy.

00:02:08.164 --> 00:02:10.162
- So he said to you,
"Expect to be beaten."

00:02:10.162 --> 00:02:11.245
- Yeah, yeah.

00:02:12.733 --> 00:02:14.108
- [Interviewer] And your
life had not been about

00:02:14.108 --> 00:02:15.081
expecting to be beaten.

00:02:15.081 --> 00:02:19.199
- No, no, so I trained
like crazy, I prepared.

00:02:19.199 --> 00:02:20.151
He did beat me in qualifying

00:02:20.151 --> 00:02:22.562
and he did beat me in the first race,

00:02:22.562 --> 00:02:25.103
but I finished just behind him in 3rd

00:02:25.103 --> 00:02:28.544
and after that, I think I
beat him in the next race.

00:02:28.544 --> 00:02:29.377
No, I didn't.

00:02:29.377 --> 00:02:31.877
I think maybe the 3rd race I beat him

00:02:31.877 --> 00:02:32.824
and then I beat him in the Championship

00:02:32.824 --> 00:02:33.657
at the end of the year.

00:02:33.657 --> 00:02:35.138
My first year, my rookie year.

00:02:35.138 --> 00:02:38.168
What I do love is when I do a race

00:02:38.168 --> 00:02:40.631
and on the edge, the whole...

00:02:40.631 --> 00:02:42.918
The last race, for example,
I was dead at the end.

00:02:42.918 --> 00:02:44.668
I was pushing so hard

00:02:47.036 --> 00:02:47.869
and really enjoying it.

00:02:47.869 --> 00:02:49.366
That's what racing's all about.

00:02:49.366 --> 00:02:50.909
I'm generally pretty hardcore.

00:02:50.909 --> 00:02:54.448
I want a hard race, I want
to be destroyed afterwards.

00:02:54.448 --> 00:02:56.230
It doesn't matter if...

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:57.063
Of course, I want to win,

00:02:57.063 --> 00:02:58.390
but as long as you've put up a good battle

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:02.676
and you've given 110%,
you've left with zero...

00:03:02.676 --> 00:03:05.056
It's not like, oh I had
couple percent left,

00:03:05.056 --> 00:03:06.526
but I finished the race.

00:03:06.526 --> 00:03:09.786
I want to be completely
depleted after a race,

00:03:09.786 --> 00:03:10.909
knowing that I gave it my all

00:03:10.909 --> 00:03:14.113
and I didn't make very many mistakes.

00:03:14.113 --> 00:03:15.386
Then I can go home proud.

00:03:15.386 --> 00:03:17.350
Unfortunately, there are
people with the talent

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:18.598
that don't have the money.

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:19.588
I kind of look at it like,

00:03:19.588 --> 00:03:20.748
if any of you've seen Cool Runnings,

00:03:20.748 --> 00:03:23.720
when they try to raise
money to go bobsledding

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:26.398
and all the people that they
approached just laughed at them

00:03:26.398 --> 00:03:28.397
and it's the same for us.

00:03:28.397 --> 00:03:31.022
My dad would say, "My
son's going to be the first

00:03:31.022 --> 00:03:31.855
"black Formula One driver",

00:03:31.855 --> 00:03:34.176
everyone thought, "Yeah right",

00:03:34.176 --> 00:03:37.414
but he kept going and it happened.

00:03:37.414 --> 00:03:40.105
We got there, so never give up.

00:03:40.105 --> 00:03:41.385
Me as a driver, I change.

00:03:41.385 --> 00:03:44.417
I improve all the time
through experiences,

00:03:44.417 --> 00:03:47.860
not just race-by-race, but in life.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.965
I'm always taking all these
different experiences,

00:03:49.965 --> 00:03:53.388
positive or negative, extracting
the best bits out of them,

00:03:53.388 --> 00:03:55.900
learning, becoming older and wiser.

00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:57.041
I'm 23 years old.

00:03:57.041 --> 00:04:00.104
I think I'm quite wise
for my age, I think.

00:04:00.104 --> 00:04:02.053
I still got a long way to go,

00:04:02.053 --> 00:04:05.315
but then, when it comes to driving,

00:04:05.315 --> 00:04:06.799
I excel.

00:04:06.799 --> 00:04:08.692
I pushed beyond limits.

00:04:08.692 --> 00:04:11.595
When I'm training, I go
beyond the pain barriers.

00:04:11.595 --> 00:04:13.586
I just do everything I can to make sure

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:16.010
that when I arrive at the race track,

00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:19.735
I've already got two,
3/10s on the other guys.

00:04:19.735 --> 00:04:23.459
I think, we as human beings, we harness...

00:04:23.459 --> 00:04:26.285
We harness energy
without even noticing it,

00:04:26.285 --> 00:04:28.654
and whether it's good or bad,

00:04:28.654 --> 00:04:33.346
and I think I harnessed all
those different experiences

00:04:33.346 --> 00:04:37.683
at school when the teachers
were negative and those parents.

00:04:37.683 --> 00:04:38.582
I just kept it

00:04:38.582 --> 00:04:41.853
and I kept it bottled inside
and I'd use it on the track.

00:04:41.853 --> 00:04:43.853
My dad would always say,

00:04:44.707 --> 00:04:46.153
'cause a kid would push me off the track

00:04:46.153 --> 00:04:47.205
and I would have aggression.

00:04:47.205 --> 00:04:50.724
I'd be like, "I want to
go and push that guy over,

00:04:50.724 --> 00:04:54.435
"or flick him in the ear,
or kick him, or something."

00:04:54.435 --> 00:04:56.600
and he would say, "Do your
talking on the track."

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:58.939
Just don't say anything, just
do your talking on the track

00:04:58.939 --> 00:05:00.420
and that applied to everything in my life,

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:02.365
so just do your talking on the track.

00:05:02.365 --> 00:05:04.949
So, I'd get on the track and I would drive

00:05:04.949 --> 00:05:06.647
the wheels off the car.

00:05:06.647 --> 00:05:10.814
When I came to Formula
One, in trying to get to...

00:05:11.694 --> 00:05:15.302
Getting into Formula One was
tough, I had to win everything.

00:05:15.302 --> 00:05:17.079
I was led to believe I had
to win every championship,

00:05:17.079 --> 00:05:20.609
so I had to make sure that
I studied about the car,

00:05:20.609 --> 00:05:21.900
everything change that I made,

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:23.294
that I had to write it down and study it.

00:05:23.294 --> 00:05:25.579
I have a catalog at home
with all the changes I made,

00:05:25.579 --> 00:05:28.664
of all my setups, so when
I got to Formula One,

00:05:28.664 --> 00:05:29.751
change the front roll bar.

00:05:29.751 --> 00:05:33.508
I know exactly what changes
that's going to make to the car.

00:05:33.508 --> 00:05:37.352
So, I had to really build
up a good understanding

00:05:37.352 --> 00:05:38.685
of mechanics and

00:05:43.414 --> 00:05:46.497
I think, when I got to McLaren,

00:05:46.497 --> 00:05:49.683
my fitness level had to take
another step, to another level.

00:05:49.683 --> 00:05:53.850
So, I was training ridiculous
amount of hours a week,

00:05:55.582 --> 00:05:58.348
which I hated. (laughs)

00:05:58.348 --> 00:06:00.356
I spent a lot of time at the factory,

00:06:00.356 --> 00:06:02.241
would sit down with an....

00:06:02.241 --> 00:06:06.896
I would have, probably
four to five, probably four

00:06:06.896 --> 00:06:10.783
engineering meetings everyday at McLaren.

00:06:10.783 --> 00:06:12.984
This was before my first season,

00:06:12.984 --> 00:06:14.115
after my GP2 season,

00:06:14.115 --> 00:06:17.190
to understand all the different scenarios,

00:06:17.190 --> 00:06:21.357
the race strategies, the
tires, the steering wheel.

00:06:22.881 --> 00:06:24.760
There was an incredible
amount of information

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:26.418
that I didn't have to do before.

00:06:26.418 --> 00:06:28.258
Before, I'd just get in the car,

00:06:28.258 --> 00:06:29.336
in Formula GP2,

00:06:29.336 --> 00:06:32.569
and I could read a couple maps,

00:06:32.569 --> 00:06:34.762
try to understand where the track's going

00:06:34.762 --> 00:06:36.593
and work with the setup,

00:06:36.593 --> 00:06:39.730
but Formula One, there's
tons and tons of information,

00:06:39.730 --> 00:06:42.614
and that was really the biggest
step that I had to make.

00:06:42.614 --> 00:06:44.649
I had a steering wheel I took
home and I had to study it.

00:06:44.649 --> 00:06:47.840
I looked at it every
morning and every evening.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:52.007
Tried to close my eyes and
know where the switches were.

00:06:53.319 --> 00:06:56.714
Obviously, just getting
up-to-speed in my first

00:06:56.714 --> 00:06:58.344
eight test days I had.

00:06:58.344 --> 00:07:01.582
Trying to get on the pace
and not make mistakes

00:07:01.582 --> 00:07:04.688
and have the fitness
level to just keep it up.

00:07:04.688 --> 00:07:05.587
That was the biggest stepping stone for me

00:07:05.587 --> 00:07:09.254
and I got to my first
race and I was fourth.

00:07:10.305 --> 00:07:11.381
I came fourth in the first race.

00:07:11.381 --> 00:07:14.580
I was ready because I really did...

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:16.505
I couldn't look back and say,

00:07:16.505 --> 00:07:17.657
"I wish I'd done some more of that"

00:07:17.657 --> 00:07:19.364
because I did everything I could.

00:07:19.364 --> 00:07:21.364
The challenge of joining

00:07:22.769 --> 00:07:24.540
Mercedes is obviously going
to a team that's struggled

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:25.832
for the last couple years.

00:07:25.832 --> 00:07:27.779
They've not won as many championships,

00:07:27.779 --> 00:07:32.743
they've not been competitive
in this era of car design.

00:07:32.743 --> 00:07:35.407
This era of car design came out in 2009

00:07:35.407 --> 00:07:38.157
and obviously you have the top three teams

00:07:38.157 --> 00:07:39.599
that have been there

00:07:39.599 --> 00:07:42.366
and now Lotus have also come
in and started competing

00:07:42.366 --> 00:07:44.643
and Mercedes finished fifth
in the Championship last year,

00:07:44.643 --> 00:07:47.252
so it's taken a team that's struggled

00:07:47.252 --> 00:07:49.705
and helping them to climb up the ladder

00:07:49.705 --> 00:07:50.538
and get higher up,

00:07:50.538 --> 00:07:51.761
so I want to be a part of that.

00:07:51.761 --> 00:07:54.323
I want to get in there and I
want to help develop a car,

00:07:54.323 --> 00:07:57.841
push it in a certain direction
I feel that I'm good at

00:07:57.841 --> 00:08:01.244
and perhaps other drivers
are not as good at maybe.

00:08:01.244 --> 00:08:04.328
Who knows, but taking
that car across a line

00:08:04.328 --> 00:08:06.927
and winning is the ultimate goal.

00:08:06.927 --> 00:08:09.344
- How do you prepare yourself

00:08:10.516 --> 00:08:12.374
to be so focused?

00:08:12.374 --> 00:08:15.457
To handle all of this massive stress?

00:08:17.156 --> 00:08:19.156
- Really, it's trying to

00:08:20.817 --> 00:08:24.097
just remain focused on the
job at hand and then the task.

00:08:24.097 --> 00:08:27.784
My goal this weekend is to win this race.

00:08:27.784 --> 00:08:30.151
All the other stuff is all just noise

00:08:30.151 --> 00:08:33.000
and I guess it's just through experience

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:34.900
being able to silence all of that

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:37.231
and stay focused on what's
the most important thing.

00:08:37.231 --> 00:08:41.398
So don't be distracted by
all the media or the cameras.

00:08:42.311 --> 00:08:44.914
Tomorrow there's so many interviews.

00:08:44.914 --> 00:08:47.063
Mostly with the same
people that we always have,

00:08:47.063 --> 00:08:51.011
so I've been talking to
these guys for 10 years,

00:08:51.011 --> 00:08:52.790
often asking the same question

00:08:52.790 --> 00:08:55.800
that they asked me two
weeks ago, but obviously

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:57.497
they have something more
to talk about this weekend

00:08:57.497 --> 00:09:00.645
because the last race was terrible.

00:09:00.645 --> 00:09:03.257
I think it really is just trying to,

00:09:03.257 --> 00:09:05.900
I guess, compartmentalize, really.

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:08.188
That stuff, put it over
here, put it in a box

00:09:08.188 --> 00:09:11.752
and then keep the energy and your focus on

00:09:11.752 --> 00:09:13.390
the one thing that matters most.

00:09:13.390 --> 00:09:15.063
All that other stuff does not matter.

00:09:15.063 --> 00:09:16.783
What matters is me and this team.

00:09:16.783 --> 00:09:20.702
How are we going to get
from Friday, or Thursday

00:09:20.702 --> 00:09:21.955
this week, for example,

00:09:21.955 --> 00:09:24.969
to Sunday, standing on top of that podium.

00:09:24.969 --> 00:09:27.542
It's sleep, it's what I eat,

00:09:27.542 --> 00:09:30.077
it's what I spend my time doing.

00:09:30.077 --> 00:09:31.641
Making sure I get to bed early.

00:09:31.641 --> 00:09:34.414
All these different
things that add up to it

00:09:34.414 --> 00:09:36.628
and sometimes you do it all
perfect and it doesn't go well,

00:09:36.628 --> 00:09:40.353
but that's life and you just hope that

00:09:40.353 --> 00:09:42.669
in doing all the right things...

00:09:42.669 --> 00:09:44.132
But it's also trying to find a balance.

00:09:44.132 --> 00:09:47.099
You need to enjoy life as well.

00:09:47.099 --> 00:09:49.540
At some stage, my career will be over

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:51.338
and I want to look back and say,

00:09:51.338 --> 00:09:53.515
"I enjoyed absolutely everything.

00:09:53.515 --> 00:09:57.050
"Every moment in the car,
every moment out of it".

00:09:57.050 --> 00:09:58.465
It's fun every time.

00:09:58.465 --> 00:10:00.385
As soon as you put your suit on, it's fun.

00:10:00.385 --> 00:10:02.912
The whole weekend's a complete blast

00:10:02.912 --> 00:10:05.632
and although it's very, very political

00:10:05.632 --> 00:10:07.837
and very serious and everything like that,

00:10:07.837 --> 00:10:12.597
which you need to because
it's immensely intense

00:10:12.597 --> 00:10:16.117
and competitive, but it's so much fun.

00:10:16.117 --> 00:10:18.754
You get in that car and I'm like a kid.

00:10:18.754 --> 00:10:20.398
I know what to do with it

00:10:20.398 --> 00:10:23.231
and I'm like a kid with a new toy.

00:10:24.477 --> 00:10:26.701
- Hello, I'm James Corden,
this is Lewis Hamilton.

00:10:26.701 --> 00:10:27.534
- Hi.

00:10:27.534 --> 00:10:30.294
- I've got one lap to ask
as many questions as I can.

00:10:30.294 --> 00:10:31.127
Lewis, are you ready?

00:10:31.127 --> 00:10:31.960
- I'm ready.

00:10:31.960 --> 00:10:33.028
- Okay.

00:10:33.028 --> 00:10:34.612
On your marks, get set.

00:10:34.612 --> 00:10:35.857
(panicked shouting)

00:10:35.857 --> 00:10:36.690
Okay!

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:37.523
Oh my God!

00:10:38.387 --> 00:10:40.079
Right, favorite film? (screams)

00:10:40.079 --> 00:10:41.270
- Coming To America.

00:10:41.270 --> 00:10:43.157
- Favorite football player?

00:10:43.157 --> 00:10:43.990
- Messi.

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:45.443
- How many crashes have you had?

00:10:45.443 --> 00:10:46.276
Oh my God!

00:10:47.786 --> 00:10:48.888
I'm asking for me, more than just--

00:10:48.888 --> 00:10:49.721
- Two.

00:10:49.721 --> 00:10:50.554
- Okay!

00:10:50.554 --> 00:10:53.627
How many pushups can you do? (screams)

00:10:53.627 --> 00:10:55.052
(laughs)

00:10:55.052 --> 00:10:56.056
- 80, 90?

00:10:56.056 --> 00:10:56.889
- Yeah, me too.

00:10:56.889 --> 00:10:57.722
90, 95.

00:10:57.722 --> 00:10:58.555
Okay.

00:10:58.555 --> 00:10:59.888
Who's your hero?

00:11:00.863 --> 00:11:01.775
- My dad.

00:11:01.775 --> 00:11:05.161
- Is there anything more
exhilarating than Formula One?

00:11:05.161 --> 00:11:06.079
- Nope!

00:11:06.079 --> 00:11:09.653
- Do you wish your
girlfriend was hot like me?

00:11:09.653 --> 00:11:10.486
(laughs)

00:11:10.486 --> 00:11:12.019
See it's ruined because he does!

00:11:12.019 --> 00:11:12.852
Oh my!

00:11:12.852 --> 00:11:13.872
Lewis!

00:11:13.872 --> 00:11:15.198
I thought you were going
to be amazing at this.

00:11:15.198 --> 00:11:17.738
We're just going over all the corners!

00:11:17.738 --> 00:11:18.602
- You sweatin' a bit?

00:11:18.602 --> 00:11:20.429
- Yes, just a touch.

00:11:20.429 --> 00:11:23.202
Right, true or false, you
wear your helmet in bed?

00:11:23.202 --> 00:11:24.422
- False.

00:11:24.422 --> 00:11:26.029
- Do you ever play with
your helmet in bed?

00:11:26.029 --> 00:11:26.862
(laughs)

00:11:26.862 --> 00:11:27.778
- If you were going to sing me a song,

00:11:27.778 --> 00:11:29.995
what song would you sing me?

00:11:29.995 --> 00:11:30.854
- Smack My Bitch Up.

00:11:30.854 --> 00:11:32.937
(laughs)

00:11:34.446 --> 00:11:35.279
- Oh my!

00:11:36.138 --> 00:11:38.221
(laughs)

00:11:39.094 --> 00:11:40.399
Okay, now okay.

00:11:40.399 --> 00:11:41.990
Oh my God!

00:11:41.990 --> 00:11:43.163
(laughs)

00:11:43.163 --> 00:11:44.858
Favorite car?

00:11:44.858 --> 00:11:45.781
- Favorite car...

00:11:45.781 --> 00:11:46.614
- Yes.

00:11:46.614 --> 00:11:47.447
- This one.

00:11:47.447 --> 00:11:48.589
- Smart or casual?

00:11:48.589 --> 00:11:49.422
- Casual.

00:11:49.422 --> 00:11:50.558
- Sebastian or Fernando?

00:11:50.558 --> 00:11:51.391
- Neither!

00:11:51.391 --> 00:11:52.224
(laughs)

00:11:52.224 --> 00:11:53.057
Go on, you've got to pick one.

00:11:53.057 --> 00:11:54.237
Sebastian or Fernando?

00:11:54.237 --> 00:11:55.070
- Fernando.

00:11:55.070 --> 00:11:58.658
- (screams) Front garden or back garden?

00:11:58.658 --> 00:12:00.610
(laughs)

00:12:00.610 --> 00:12:01.443
Oh my God!

00:12:02.351 --> 00:12:03.351
Come on now.

00:12:04.397 --> 00:12:06.085
Do you still get parking tickets?

00:12:06.085 --> 00:12:06.918
- Nope.

00:12:06.918 --> 00:12:07.751
- What do you wear to bed?

00:12:07.751 --> 00:12:08.584
(mumbles)

00:12:08.584 --> 00:12:09.417
What is the best city in the world?

00:12:09.417 --> 00:12:10.250
- London.

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:11.641
Punch the brakes!

00:12:11.641 --> 00:12:14.574
(shouts) Oh my God!

00:12:14.574 --> 00:12:16.224
- Boxers.

00:12:16.224 --> 00:12:18.474
- Whoa, what you doing now?

00:12:19.416 --> 00:12:21.013
(screams)

00:12:21.013 --> 00:12:22.346
Oh, come on now.

00:12:25.383 --> 00:12:27.383
(sighs)

00:12:30.746 --> 00:12:31.579
Oh my--

00:12:31.579 --> 00:12:32.412
- We're done, man!

00:12:32.412 --> 00:12:33.245
- Thank you!

00:12:33.245 --> 00:12:34.662
That was amazing!

00:12:38.938 --> 00:12:42.105
I can't feel my legs, it's ridiculous.

00:12:44.188 --> 00:12:45.733
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:12:45.733 --> 00:12:48.209
I made this video because
Lagmin asked me to.

00:12:48.209 --> 00:12:49.220
So if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:12:49.220 --> 00:12:50.974
that you want me to profile next,

00:12:50.974 --> 00:12:52.157
leave it in the comments below

00:12:52.157 --> 00:12:53.369
and I'll see what I can do.

00:12:53.369 --> 00:12:54.202
I'd also love to know,

00:12:54.202 --> 00:12:57.478
what did Lewis say that really
resonated the most with you?

00:12:57.478 --> 00:12:59.794
What is going to have the
biggest impact on your life,

00:12:59.794 --> 00:13:02.526
or your business after
watching this video?

00:13:02.526 --> 00:13:04.660
Leave your thoughts in the comments below.

00:13:04.660 --> 00:13:06.345
I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:13:06.345 --> 00:13:08.936
Finally, I want to give a quick
shout-out to Gaella Kaneza.

00:13:08.936 --> 00:13:11.988
Thank you so much, Gaella, for
picking up a copy of my book.

00:13:11.988 --> 00:13:14.718
It really, really, really,
really means a lot to me.

00:13:14.718 --> 00:13:16.076
Thank you guys, again, for watching.

00:13:16.076 --> 00:13:17.423
I believe in you.

00:13:17.423 --> 00:13:19.896
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:13:19.896 --> 00:13:22.007
and whatever your one word is.

00:13:22.007 --> 00:13:23.259
Much love!

00:13:23.259 --> 00:13:24.759
I'll see you soon.

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:31.945
- When you're building up to Formula One,

00:13:31.945 --> 00:13:33.383
you're obviously preparing to race,

00:13:33.383 --> 00:13:34.216
but you're not prepared for

00:13:34.216 --> 00:13:37.463
what comes along with
being a Formula One driver.

00:13:37.463 --> 00:13:40.963
The pressure of such a big team, sponsors,

00:13:41.860 --> 00:13:45.189
media, sitting on stage, talking.

00:13:45.189 --> 00:13:46.078
You're not prepared for that.

00:13:46.078 --> 00:13:47.622
You're not put through a school,

00:13:47.622 --> 00:13:49.378
or through other interviews for it,

00:13:49.378 --> 00:13:53.921
so you arrive in the deep end
without being able to swim.

00:13:53.921 --> 00:13:55.320
I made a lot of mistakes.

00:13:55.320 --> 00:13:56.404
I got into...

00:13:56.404 --> 00:13:58.331
obviously, I was quick on track.

00:13:58.331 --> 00:14:01.363
That was the easy part,
is everything outside,

00:14:01.363 --> 00:14:05.280
but I lost the first year
in 2007 by one point,

00:14:06.744 --> 00:14:11.497
which was, depending on how
serious you take your job,

00:14:11.497 --> 00:14:14.277
it was emotionally
traumatizing the first year.

00:14:14.277 --> 00:14:15.619
Came back the next year,

00:14:15.619 --> 00:14:18.786
somehow I came through that experience

00:14:20.042 --> 00:14:23.808
and then in that last
race I had to finish 5th.

00:14:23.808 --> 00:14:25.981
I started third, I think it was

00:14:25.981 --> 00:14:29.656
and that was fourth, fifth and
then, probably like six laps,

00:14:29.656 --> 00:14:32.927
seven laps to go, I was down in sixth

00:14:32.927 --> 00:14:35.618
and the guy that was ahead
of me was Sebastian Vettel

00:14:35.618 --> 00:14:36.951
and there was...

00:14:40.522 --> 00:14:42.878
If I couldn't do anything
even to save my mother's life

00:14:42.878 --> 00:14:45.100
and my mom was over there
on the edge of the cliff,

00:14:45.100 --> 00:14:46.361
I had to pass him in order to.

00:14:46.361 --> 00:14:48.859
I couldn't get past him!

00:14:48.859 --> 00:14:50.450
I couldn't get past this guy

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:53.014
and for those laps, I
just wasn't giving up,

00:14:53.014 --> 00:14:56.447
but I could see that dream fading away

00:14:56.447 --> 00:14:58.692
and then the last lap,

00:14:58.692 --> 00:15:01.496
some guy was on slick
tires, I was on wets.

00:15:01.496 --> 00:15:04.783
He was stumbling, quite a
few of them were stumbling.

00:15:04.783 --> 00:15:06.206
I was overtaking cars here and there,

00:15:06.206 --> 00:15:07.966
I had no idea where I was.

00:15:07.966 --> 00:15:10.046
I thought they were backmarkers.

00:15:10.046 --> 00:15:12.566
The guy came across the
line and thought he had,

00:15:12.566 --> 00:15:14.704
for a second, was World Champion

00:15:14.704 --> 00:15:17.541
and then I came across
the line 17 seconds later

00:15:17.541 --> 00:15:18.884
and I crossed the line

00:15:18.884 --> 00:15:20.551
and I thought I lost
the World Championships,

00:15:20.551 --> 00:15:21.968
so my heart sunk.

00:15:23.233 --> 00:15:25.514
I was distraught and then,

00:15:25.514 --> 00:15:26.711
I don't know why they took so long,

00:15:26.711 --> 00:15:28.358
but like 12, 13 seconds later,

00:15:28.358 --> 00:15:31.527
they told me I was World Champion.

00:15:31.527 --> 00:15:33.883
I didn't know what the hell was going on.

00:15:33.883 --> 00:15:34.739
I think it just at the time,

00:15:34.739 --> 00:15:39.324
after that big whirlwind of
media, back at the factory,

00:15:39.324 --> 00:15:41.015
there was so much tension.

00:15:41.015 --> 00:15:45.622
I guess, I was just only 23,
so I just don't feel I was...

00:15:45.622 --> 00:15:47.202
Don't forget, growing up,

00:15:47.202 --> 00:15:49.220
instead of hanging out with
friends on the weekends

00:15:49.220 --> 00:15:53.661
and doing normal kid social
life stuff, I was racing.

00:15:53.661 --> 00:15:57.095
I was with adults, so I missed that a lot.

00:15:57.095 --> 00:15:58.774
That maturity growing up stage

00:15:58.774 --> 00:16:01.433
and I don't feel I was mature
enough to really be able

00:16:01.433 --> 00:16:03.918
to embrace the whole
experience and enjoy it.

00:16:03.918 --> 00:16:05.491
So, I tell you, it was not a great..

00:16:05.491 --> 00:16:07.268
Whilst it's amazing that
I won the Championship,

00:16:07.268 --> 00:16:08.314
it just wasn't--

00:16:08.314 --> 00:16:10.247
I wasn't able to enjoy it.

00:16:10.247 --> 00:16:11.832
Rolled into the second year.

00:16:11.832 --> 00:16:13.326
The year after that for example,

00:16:13.326 --> 00:16:15.633
but the last two
Championships have really,

00:16:15.633 --> 00:16:17.246
I guess, coming of an age,

00:16:17.246 --> 00:16:19.307
been able to really absorb
it and enjoy the moment

00:16:19.307 --> 00:16:22.652
because so much work has
gone in from my family,

00:16:22.652 --> 00:16:24.727
so I don't take it for granted,

00:16:24.727 --> 00:16:27.895
the opportunity that I have, for one.

00:16:27.895 --> 00:16:30.350
There are so many people
that would cut their leg off

00:16:30.350 --> 00:16:33.183
to be in my seat and do what I do.

00:16:34.052 --> 00:16:37.479
So I make sure that I maximize
every time I get in the car.

00:16:37.479 --> 00:16:40.043
I'm representing my family
every time I get in that car

00:16:40.043 --> 00:16:42.126
and so there's nothing...

00:16:43.933 --> 00:16:46.683
there's no time for second place.

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:50.445
Of course, those experiences,
when you have those lows,

00:16:50.445 --> 00:16:53.178
like losing the World Championship,

00:16:53.178 --> 00:16:54.695
only make you stronger when you do,

00:16:54.695 --> 00:16:58.045
or realize that there's highs and lows.

00:16:58.045 --> 00:16:59.068
See, once you've had the low,

00:16:59.068 --> 00:17:01.533
you appreciate the highs even more.

00:17:01.533 --> 00:17:02.366
- It's presumably particularly

00:17:02.366 --> 00:17:04.297
frustrating for you this season.

00:17:04.297 --> 00:17:05.792
It's early days yet, but--

00:17:05.792 --> 00:17:06.745
- It's a killer season.

00:17:06.745 --> 00:17:10.474
It's terrible (laughs)

00:17:10.474 --> 00:17:14.242
Obviously, I had a couple of
amazing years, the last two.

00:17:14.242 --> 00:17:16.063
I would say this is...

00:17:16.063 --> 00:17:20.358
Luckily, through the experience
of the 10 years of racing,

00:17:20.358 --> 00:17:22.607
you have the ups and downs
and I definitely think

00:17:22.607 --> 00:17:25.562
these past five races have been

00:17:25.562 --> 00:17:27.140
massively testing for myself,

00:17:27.140 --> 00:17:29.303
my mechanics, for my engineers.

00:17:29.303 --> 00:17:31.556
I think each time, I see
it as a challenge to rise.

00:17:31.556 --> 00:17:33.143
I see it as a challenge to...

00:17:33.143 --> 00:17:34.543
I'm going to be facing
the media right now,

00:17:34.543 --> 00:17:35.629
but I feel terrible.

00:17:35.629 --> 00:17:36.876
I'm angry that I lost the race,

00:17:36.876 --> 00:17:37.988
or something like that,

00:17:37.988 --> 00:17:41.757
but it's a moment for me to,
the kids that are watching,

00:17:41.757 --> 00:17:43.163
to me to say the right things.

00:17:43.163 --> 00:17:45.926
It's a moment for me to lift my guys up,

00:17:45.926 --> 00:17:48.081
who are probably feeling
just as much as me,

00:17:48.081 --> 00:17:51.867
or back at the factory, who
work nonstop to build my car.

00:17:51.867 --> 00:17:54.200
So, there's so much going on

00:17:55.734 --> 00:17:58.734
and I feel often when I do it right,

00:18:00.418 --> 00:18:01.963
I come out of it so much stronger

00:18:01.963 --> 00:18:05.523
and so, I do feel this is
just trials and tribulations.

00:18:05.523 --> 00:18:09.251
This is a period of time
of growth for me that,

00:18:09.251 --> 00:18:11.154
whilst there's always growth--

00:18:11.154 --> 00:18:13.237
I met Nelson Mandela once

00:18:15.274 --> 00:18:16.107
when he was 90,

00:18:16.107 --> 00:18:16.940
for his 90th birthday,

00:18:16.940 --> 00:18:19.810
and he said to me that he was
still learning at that time.

00:18:19.810 --> 00:18:23.528
So, I have a long way to go, hopefully.

00:18:23.528 --> 00:18:27.528
I think the advice that
I would give would be to

00:18:29.311 --> 00:18:33.090
try and get much running as you can.

00:18:33.090 --> 00:18:34.590
Take your time and

00:18:36.003 --> 00:18:38.019
it's so easy to just get ahead of yourself

00:18:38.019 --> 00:18:40.191
and think, "I'm ready for this,

00:18:40.191 --> 00:18:41.781
"I'm ready to take the next step."

00:18:41.781 --> 00:18:42.753
and you just got to take your time.

00:18:42.753 --> 00:18:46.402
That was really the fortunate thing

00:18:46.402 --> 00:18:48.132
I had with all of my support,

00:18:48.132 --> 00:18:51.799
from my dad and from
Ron, was just trying to

00:18:53.101 --> 00:18:55.222
make sure that we didn't rush it

00:18:55.222 --> 00:18:57.488
and you just take your time,

00:18:57.488 --> 00:18:59.884
get lots and lots of
miles under your belt,

00:18:59.884 --> 00:19:04.615
lots of racing experience,
wheel-to-wheel racing,

00:19:04.615 --> 00:19:07.468
and utilize every second you get on track.

00:19:07.468 --> 00:19:09.176
I do everything.

00:19:09.176 --> 00:19:11.884
I love jet skiing, going out
on quad bikes, motor bikes,

00:19:11.884 --> 00:19:15.330
surfing, rock climbing, pretty
much anything with an engine.

00:19:15.330 --> 00:19:16.887
Yeah, I try to do as many things as I can.

00:19:16.887 --> 00:19:19.561
I like to do water skiing,
I like to do wakeboarding

00:19:19.561 --> 00:19:23.090
and monoskiing, so I pretty
much do quite a few things,

00:19:23.090 --> 00:19:25.176
but those are the things that I do too.

00:19:25.176 --> 00:19:26.195
And my dad would be like,

00:19:26.195 --> 00:19:28.007
"You shouldn't be doing
any of those things

00:19:28.007 --> 00:19:29.800
"'cause you race a Formula
One car, you don't need to.",

00:19:29.800 --> 00:19:31.506
but when you're not
racing, you need something

00:19:31.506 --> 00:19:33.951
to keep that adrenaline
and that hunger going.

